" VIM:vimrc - AmiBash's system-wide settings for Vim on AmigaOS.
" Your own settings go in S:.vimrc, VIM:.vimrc or HOME:.vimrc.

" Amiga screens and fonts are Latin-1, files today are often UTF-8: keep
" text as UTF-8 inside Vim, read UTF-8 or Latin-1 files as they are, show
" them in Latin-1 (characters it lacks appear as ?) and write new files
" in Latin-1 like other Amiga programs.
set encoding=utf-8
set termencoding=latin1
set fileencodings=ucs-bom,utf-8,latin1
setglobal fileencoding=latin1
